1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:02,010
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:02,010 --> 00:00:03,480
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:07,750
(Episode 23)

4
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:17,560
Mom.

5
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:19,090
Mom.

6
00:00:20,330 --> 00:00:21,660
Is it just my imagination?

7
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:23,860
It probably is,

8
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:26,830
but it definitely smells
like Mom's embrace.

9
00:00:27,470 --> 00:00:28,800
It's exactly the same.

10
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:31,100
Oh, right.

11
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:47,250
Who...

12
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:48,750
Who is this?

13
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:50,860
Right.

14
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:54,090
My eyes are still perfectly fine.

15
00:00:54,330 --> 00:00:55,830
I'm glad I caught you.

16
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:57,430
You stand right there.

17
00:00:57,830 --> 00:01:00,570
No, you have the wrong person.

18
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:03,440
I came to the wrong house, ma'am.

19
00:01:04,370 --> 00:01:07,770
If I let you slip away this time,
my name is not Choi Soon Deok.

20
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:09,940
Our family is famous
for being relentless,

21
00:01:09,940 --> 00:01:11,640
and we have the pedigree
to prove it.

22
00:01:11,910 --> 00:01:14,010
Are you not going to stop? You punk.

23
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:24,760
Gosh. It's been 20 years,

24
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:27,060
and you haven't lost your touch
at all, Mother.

25
00:01:29,530 --> 00:01:32,300
Stop right there, you punk.
Kang Hak Sung!

26
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,430
That little...

27
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:36,600
- Why that little...
- Mom.

28
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:38,540
- Darn it.
- Mom.

29
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:50,750
Thank you, Dr. Ju.

30
00:01:52,250 --> 00:01:53,250
Please go to the examination room...

31
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:54,620
and get your blood pressure
checked first,

32
00:01:55,350 --> 00:01:57,860
and I'd like to give you
some treatment, Ms. Jo.

33
00:01:57,960 --> 00:01:59,290
You look very pale.

34
00:01:59,690 --> 00:02:01,630
Well, I've been...

35
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:03,260
dealing with
some stressful matters lately...

36
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:06,730
Thank you, but I'm fine.

37
00:02:07,370 --> 00:02:08,370
I just need a moment.

38
00:02:15,870 --> 00:02:18,210
How about getting an IV drip
before you go?

39
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:19,810
Your health comes first.

40
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:23,380
I feel better now.

41
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:27,190
Oh, by the way,

42
00:02:27,990 --> 00:02:30,150
about the handkerchief you gave me
at the real estate agency last time.

43
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:31,890
I need to return it to you.

44
00:02:32,590 --> 00:02:33,960
That's okay.

45
00:02:34,660 --> 00:02:36,900
It's made of really good material.

46
00:02:37,830 --> 00:02:40,030
I'll wash it nicely and return it.

47
00:02:41,330 --> 00:02:43,840
They say experience
is the best teacher,

48
00:02:44,170 --> 00:02:46,500
and since my daughter dreams
of becoming a fashion designer,

49
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:48,570
I know a thing or two
about fabrics myself.

50
00:02:49,570 --> 00:02:50,910
I see.

51
00:02:51,410 --> 00:02:54,150
If she looks like you,
she must be beautiful.

52
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:58,780
She's the prettiest girl
in the world.

53
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:00,550
In my eyes.

54
00:03:02,890 --> 00:03:05,220
Thank you. I should get going now.

55
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:08,730
Take your time.

56
00:03:09,030 --> 00:03:10,230
Yes.

57
00:03:17,070 --> 00:03:19,340
Please come by anytime
if you feel unwell.

58
00:03:36,990 --> 00:03:38,320
What? What's going on?

59
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,790
Why am I getting butterflies?

60
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:46,100
Wait, but those two,
are they allowed to do that?

61
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:48,900
Ms. Jo and our director...

62
00:03:50,030 --> 00:03:51,240
Are they allowed to do that?

63
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:16,160
Why did you have to fall
right there of all places?

64
00:04:16,390 --> 00:04:18,330
I really thought something bad
had happened to you, Mother,

65
00:04:18,330 --> 00:04:19,800
and it scared me to death.

66
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:22,130
Do you think you were
as shocked as I was?

67
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:23,940
My goodness.

68
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:26,170
This is unbelievable.

69
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:28,840
You had such a great job,

70
00:04:28,970 --> 00:04:30,810
so where did you throw
all your money away?

71
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:33,280
How did your life end up
in such a miserable state?

72
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:35,450
It's truly a shame
that I'm the only one seeing this.

73
00:04:40,150 --> 00:04:42,920
Would you like some water?
I'm incredibly thirsty.

74
00:04:42,990 --> 00:04:44,760
How do you have the nerve
to show your face here?

75
00:04:46,990 --> 00:04:48,030
Mother.

76
00:04:52,230 --> 00:04:53,260
Mom.

77
00:04:54,570 --> 00:04:55,870
You rotten jerk.

78
00:04:56,570 --> 00:04:57,900
Look at the state of you
right now...

79
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:00,140
Haven't you even
been eating properly?

80
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:07,910
It seems...

81
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:10,420
Mi Mi has been taking good care
of you, Mother.

82
00:05:11,250 --> 00:05:13,020
You're as beautiful as ever.

83
00:05:14,750 --> 00:05:16,150
Don't give me that nonsense.

84
00:05:17,090 --> 00:05:18,520
It serves you right.

85
00:05:18,990 --> 00:05:21,660
It's so refreshing to see you
come back completely ruined.

86
00:05:21,990 --> 00:05:25,360
But don't ever show your face
near our house again.

87
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:26,360
Do you understand?

88
00:05:26,530 --> 00:05:28,730
I only came here to tell you that.

89
00:05:29,330 --> 00:05:32,270
I worked so hard to protect
my family and my children.

90
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:34,010
So get lost!

91
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:35,970
Did you hear me?

92
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:46,820
Look at the pathetic way you live.

93
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:50,660
Come on, Mom.

94
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:52,020
Mom?

95
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:54,130
In your dreams!

96
00:05:58,130 --> 00:05:59,130
Mom...

97
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,870
Goodness.

98
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:18,680
Where in the world have you been?

99
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:21,250
I haven't had a second to rest
getting ready for the dinner rush!

100
00:06:21,420 --> 00:06:23,290
You already left me to handle
the lunch crowd all by myself.

101
00:06:24,190 --> 00:06:27,060
I'm sorry. I'll come out
after lying down for a little bit.

102
00:06:27,790 --> 00:06:28,790
Mi Mi.

103
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:31,760
What is it?

104
00:06:32,230 --> 00:06:34,100
I told you I'll be out
in a little bit.

105
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:40,070
I know you're worried sick about
Gang Nam and Dae Chi,

106
00:06:40,470 --> 00:06:43,340
but Mrs. Choi already sorted
everything out, didn't she?

107
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:46,280
Stop agonizing over it
and just let it go.

108
00:06:46,340 --> 00:06:48,380
You're going to worry yourself
to death at this rate.

109
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:52,350
Dae Chi is very capable.
He has a great job.

110
00:06:52,550 --> 00:06:54,650
He'll get back on his feet
in no time.

111
00:06:54,790 --> 00:06:57,090
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

112
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:59,590
Leave out the ginseng
that's sliced too thin...

113
00:06:59,660 --> 00:07:01,190
and only pick out
the good pieces to put in.

114
00:07:01,730 --> 00:07:02,860
The customers don't like it.

115
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:10,670
Well, looking at it this way,

116
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:12,800
I'm the lucky one
for not having children.

117
00:07:13,570 --> 00:07:16,670
If you have them,
they give you headaches,

118
00:07:16,740 --> 00:07:18,380
and if you don't, you feel empty.

119
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:48,210
Hi, Mom. What is it?

120
00:07:49,610 --> 00:07:51,510
Hi, Da Mi.

121
00:07:52,510 --> 00:07:53,640
Are you going to be very late today?

122
00:07:54,610 --> 00:07:55,610
When are you coming home?

123
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:59,480
I think I'll be a little late.
Why? Is something wrong?

124
00:08:00,350 --> 00:08:01,350
No.

125
00:08:02,390 --> 00:08:03,420
It's just...

126
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:08,530
This morning, you said...

127
00:08:09,230 --> 00:08:11,500
if I had something to say,
I should just be direct about it.

128
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:16,130
So I'm going to be direct.

129
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,610
Da Mi, the truth is...

130
00:08:23,010 --> 00:08:25,340
Mom has something
to tell you in person.

131
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:30,050
I had a feeling. Okay, Mom,

132
00:08:30,110 --> 00:08:31,620
I'll try to get home
as early as possible.

133
00:08:32,050 --> 00:08:33,450
Stay awake and wait for me.

134
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:38,160
Okay, see you later, sweetie.
Watch out for cars.

135
00:08:41,890 --> 00:08:42,890
Da Mi.

136
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:44,760
Are you listening?

137
00:08:47,930 --> 00:08:50,070
I got it. I'm hanging up.

138
00:09:07,250 --> 00:09:09,850
(Da Mi's Wedding Fund)

139
00:09:09,850 --> 00:09:14,060
(Cashier's Check 10,000 Dollars)

140
00:09:29,570 --> 00:09:31,210
(Daeyang Bank)

141
00:09:31,210 --> 00:09:34,810
(Regular Payment 200 Dollars,
Total 80,000 Dollars)

142
00:10:08,410 --> 00:10:10,650
Goodness.

143
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,950
That good-for-nothing jerk.

144
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:41,680
So he's still alive.

145
00:10:43,050 --> 00:10:45,950
At least he's alive.

146
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,770
Is she at home instead of
getting ready for the dinner rush?

147
00:11:06,140 --> 00:11:07,300
Mi Mi.

148
00:11:20,550 --> 00:11:22,690
You might as well
just close the shop.

149
00:11:25,290 --> 00:11:26,290
Mother.

150
00:11:27,290 --> 00:11:29,730
If you just lie there crying,

151
00:11:29,860 --> 00:11:32,160
will money fall from the sky?
Will rice?

152
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:34,400
Are you just going
to count on your sister...

153
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:35,600
and lie there forever?

154
00:11:36,230 --> 00:11:38,240
I'm sorry,
my body just feels a bit heavy.

155
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:39,970
I'll head out.

156
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:42,410
Living under the same roof
as your old mother-in-law,

157
00:11:42,470 --> 00:11:44,710
and you're lying on your back
before the sun even sets.

158
00:11:45,180 --> 00:11:47,410
I guess you're getting older, too.

159
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:49,880
Showing a side of yourself
I've never seen.

160
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:07,630
But why is Mother so angry?

161
00:12:09,430 --> 00:12:11,870
Did she see something upsetting
while she was out?

162
00:12:21,410 --> 00:12:24,480
Don't speak out of anger.
Just stay calm, okay?

163
00:12:25,050 --> 00:12:27,220
I mean, why in the world
is she acting like this?

164
00:12:27,820 --> 00:12:29,220
Wait, is her mind slipping again?

165
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:32,190
Don't say things like that.

166
00:12:32,890 --> 00:12:34,660
It'll be fine if we explain it well.

167
00:12:35,190 --> 00:12:37,390
I'm right here with you. Let's go.

168
00:12:41,170 --> 00:12:42,970
She said not to let anyone in.

169
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:44,800
It's because we have
something urgent to tell her.

170
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:47,270
- You can't go in.
- Please step aside.

171
00:12:47,610 --> 00:12:49,910
If anyone gets scolded, it'll be me,
so just open the door...

172
00:12:49,910 --> 00:12:51,910
Why is it so noisy out there?

173
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:55,750
Mother, we'll explain everything.

174
00:12:55,810 --> 00:12:58,220
Let's come in first
so we can talk...

175
00:12:58,280 --> 00:13:00,250
Until I give my permission,

176
00:13:00,550 --> 00:13:03,650
don't even think about stepping
one foot inside this room!

177
00:13:04,290 --> 00:13:05,290
Mother.

178
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:20,200
Honey, what are you doing?

179
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:23,540
Until you're no longer upset,
I'll wait right here.

180
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:55,170
- What's going on, Mrs. Anseong?
- I'll bring up whatever you need.

181
00:13:55,410 --> 00:13:58,180
Did something happen?

182
00:13:58,480 --> 00:14:00,110
Well, you see...

183
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:02,780
I'll bring up what you need.

184
00:14:03,110 --> 00:14:07,450
Oh, okay.
Then please bring me some water.

185
00:14:16,030 --> 00:14:18,100
How many days will this storm last?

186
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:19,930
It's so annoying.

187
00:14:29,370 --> 00:14:30,370
You're here?

188
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:31,980
Did you see? What is it?
What's going on?

189
00:14:32,910 --> 00:14:34,180
Why do you want to know?

190
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:40,020
It's between the adults,

191
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:41,790
so let's just pretend
we don't know for now.

192
00:14:43,050 --> 00:14:44,360
We're adults too, you know.

193
00:14:45,690 --> 00:14:46,690
Okay.

194
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:56,700
Did someone go and poke
our sleeping lion, Madam Hwang?

195
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,410
Hey, Cha Se Na.

196
00:15:01,810 --> 00:15:02,810
What?

197
00:15:02,870 --> 00:15:06,080
Do you happen to keep in touch
with Manager Kang?

198
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:09,280
Manager Kang?
Oh, you must mean Da Mi.

199
00:15:09,850 --> 00:15:11,280
Since when were you two so close?

200
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:15,490
Well, it's for work.
I have a proposal for her,

201
00:15:15,550 --> 00:15:18,190
so I was going to contact her
about business.

202
00:15:19,090 --> 00:15:21,430
Could you ask her when she's free?

203
00:15:21,930 --> 00:15:24,800
What business? What proposal?

204
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:26,830
Hey, Cha Do Yun.

205
00:15:27,030 --> 00:15:29,800
Do you happen to have
ulterior motives for Da Mi?

206
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,200
What?

207
00:15:31,870 --> 00:15:32,940
What nonsense is that?

208
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:36,870
You totally do.
No way, absolutely not.

209
00:15:36,870 --> 00:15:38,340
She's too good for you.
I won't do it.

210
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:41,750
Fine, don't. I'll handle it myself.

211
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:45,850
So you do know
Manager Kang's number, right?

212
00:15:45,850 --> 00:15:46,850
Are you an idiot?

213
00:15:47,020 --> 00:15:48,690
How else would I have
booked the fitting?

214
00:15:49,150 --> 00:15:50,920
If it's for work,
you can just contact her directly.

215
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:52,760
Why go out of your way
to ask through me?

216
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:56,860
Now that I think about it,
this was all planned.

217
00:15:57,190 --> 00:15:59,160
What? Hey, Cha Se Na, you...

218
00:16:08,370 --> 00:16:09,510
(No clear design focus)

219
00:16:10,070 --> 00:16:11,340
(Distracting draping folds on chest)

220
00:16:16,310 --> 00:16:17,380
How should I tell her?

221
00:16:28,990 --> 00:16:31,930
Why is it so hard to see
your face these days, sweetie?

222
00:16:32,230 --> 00:16:34,500
I guess it's because
I became a working mom.

223
00:16:34,570 --> 00:16:36,030
- Right?
- Oh, right.

224
00:16:36,430 --> 00:16:38,100
Mom, is the hospital work
manageable?

225
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,170
Yes, the work is fine.

226
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,370
- But the location is a bit...
- The location?

227
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:44,910
You said you liked it
because it was close to home.

228
00:16:45,310 --> 00:16:47,750
No, it's nothing.

229
00:16:48,010 --> 00:16:51,950
By the way, are things progressing
with the CEO's son at the company?

230
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:55,520
Whenever I think I'm scoring points
with CEO Jeon,

231
00:16:55,890 --> 00:16:58,160
it feels like I'm losing points
with him.

232
00:16:58,360 --> 00:16:59,660
Why would you lose points?

233
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:01,490
Because of what?
What does my daughter lack?

234
00:17:02,030 --> 00:17:03,190
It's nothing major.

235
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:05,130
I think I just had
a slip of the tongue.

236
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:06,200
What?

237
00:17:07,730 --> 00:17:10,670
It's hard to succeed
with a single word,

238
00:17:10,730 --> 00:17:12,100
but it's easy to ruin
everything, sweetie.

239
00:17:12,170 --> 00:17:13,700
You really have to be careful.

240
00:17:13,870 --> 00:17:15,170
Is that what you've learned
from experience, Mom?

241
00:17:15,810 --> 00:17:17,370
Gosh, well...

242
00:17:18,010 --> 00:17:21,680
It never hurts to be careful
with both your words and actions.

243
00:17:22,350 --> 00:17:23,550
Hurry up and wash so we can eat.

244
00:17:23,610 --> 00:17:27,080
It's been a while since I've had
a nice, quiet meal with my daughter.

245
00:17:27,550 --> 00:17:29,720
- What about Dad?
- I don't know.

246
00:17:29,950 --> 00:17:32,120
He was chugging soju
early in the evening for some reason,

247
00:17:32,290 --> 00:17:33,320
and now he's passed out.

248
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:48,310
Hak Sung.

249
00:17:49,210 --> 00:17:51,610
Hak Sung. Honey, wake up.

250
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:53,840
You should eat dinner
before sleeping.

251
00:17:54,780 --> 00:17:56,210
You reek of alcohol.

252
00:17:56,810 --> 00:17:57,820
Mother.

253
00:17:58,720 --> 00:17:59,720
Mom.

254
00:18:01,050 --> 00:18:02,820
What? Who?

255
00:18:03,850 --> 00:18:07,390
I missed you. Mother.

256
00:18:09,030 --> 00:18:11,430
This man, seriously. Honey.

257
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:13,700
Honey, wake up.

258
00:18:14,130 --> 00:18:15,530
Yes, I'll definitely...

259
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:18,670
get back on my feet. Yes.

260
00:18:19,270 --> 00:18:20,970
I'll definitely get back on my feet.

261
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:22,310
Just...

262
00:18:23,410 --> 00:18:24,940
watch me.

263
00:18:25,140 --> 00:18:26,140
Mom.

264
00:18:26,610 --> 00:18:28,850
- Mom.
- Unbelievable, seriously.

265
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:46,800
How long has it been?

266
00:18:47,630 --> 00:18:49,670
It's been about
two and a half hours.

267
00:18:49,830 --> 00:18:51,400
Are they still out there?

268
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:53,140
Yes, they are.

269
00:18:59,140 --> 00:19:00,440
Tell them to come in.

270
00:19:07,450 --> 00:19:08,450
Who is it?

271
00:19:09,050 --> 00:19:10,890
If it's Cha Do Yun, go away.

272
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:13,020
What about Cha Seung Yun?

273
00:19:13,290 --> 00:19:14,960
What? Seung Yun?

274
00:19:16,430 --> 00:19:17,430
Come in.

275
00:19:27,770 --> 00:19:28,910
I have something to ask you.

276
00:19:29,940 --> 00:19:32,180
But first, look at my new design.

277
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:36,050
I was inspired by
a pretty woman I saw.

278
00:19:37,150 --> 00:19:38,150
Does it look okay?

279
00:19:40,550 --> 00:19:41,850
Yes, it looks pretty good,

280
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:44,960
but it might be a little uncomfortable
to actually wear.

281
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:50,790
Okay.
Then I'll reduce the lace a bit...

282
00:19:50,790 --> 00:19:53,030
and widen the ends...

283
00:19:55,130 --> 00:19:57,100
Right, what did you want to ask me?

284
00:19:58,170 --> 00:19:59,700
Well, I wanted to...

285
00:20:01,840 --> 00:20:03,110
Can you...

286
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:06,380
Mother,

287
00:20:06,980 --> 00:20:08,950
I know this will sound
like an excuse, but...

288
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:11,920
I did it for our group's image...

289
00:20:13,820 --> 00:20:14,820
I'm sorry.

290
00:20:16,250 --> 00:20:20,490
My husband did nothing wrong.
I handled everything on my own.

291
00:20:20,560 --> 00:20:22,790
It's all my fault, Mother.

292
00:20:22,990 --> 00:20:24,390
Please punish me.

293
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:30,270
Jin Hee, raise your head.

294
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:36,510
It was clearly under the name
of Hwanggeum Capital...

295
00:20:37,540 --> 00:20:40,640
that the promotional article
was published,

296
00:20:41,310 --> 00:20:45,120
so even though you took the lead
and spearheaded it,

297
00:20:45,750 --> 00:20:47,880
in the end, it's not your fault.

298
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:51,090
It's the incompetence
of a husband...

299
00:20:51,390 --> 00:20:52,820
who couldn't keep his wife in check.

300
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:55,530
That's why I...

301
00:20:55,590 --> 00:20:58,360
removed my son
from his position as CEO.

302
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:01,670
In Sung.

303
00:21:02,370 --> 00:21:03,700
Do you have anything else to say?

304
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:09,140
No, Mother. It's all my fault.

305
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:12,880
I was wrong, Mother.

306
00:21:14,410 --> 00:21:15,610
I'm exhausted.

307
00:21:17,110 --> 00:21:18,550
You may leave now.

308
00:21:28,230 --> 00:21:29,230
What is it?

309
00:21:29,990 --> 00:21:32,400
Consider it payback
for the tutoring you gave me,

310
00:21:32,460 --> 00:21:33,600
and I'll answer anything.

311
00:21:35,900 --> 00:21:37,130
You know Kang Da Mi, right?

312
00:21:37,630 --> 00:21:39,200
Da Mi?

313
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,510
Could you give me
her contact information?

314
00:21:43,110 --> 00:21:46,840
Why do you need to contact Da Mi?

315
00:21:48,110 --> 00:21:49,310
Just for work.

316
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:51,480
All right.

317
00:21:59,560 --> 00:22:00,560
I sent it.

318
00:22:03,830 --> 00:22:04,830
What?

319
00:22:05,860 --> 00:22:07,030
No, it's nothing.

320
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:08,500
Okay.

321
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:11,200
- Thanks.
- No problem.

322
00:22:27,620 --> 00:22:29,920
I'm sorry for making you wait
so long, Su Ah.

323
00:22:30,050 --> 00:22:32,190
Dad must have had an emergency.

324
00:22:32,620 --> 00:22:36,060
I'm still really glad
because you came to pick me up.

325
00:22:36,960 --> 00:22:40,200
But it seems like
you're walking a bit slower, Su Ah.

326
00:22:40,700 --> 00:22:42,770
- Do your legs hurt?
- No.

327
00:22:42,830 --> 00:22:44,300
Are you tired, then?

328
00:22:45,370 --> 00:22:48,610
I just wanted to take my time
before I have to say goodbye to you.

329
00:22:56,180 --> 00:22:57,250
Oh, my baby.

330
00:22:57,850 --> 00:23:00,020
Mom will come see you often.

331
00:23:01,750 --> 00:23:03,490
- Let's go inside.
- Okay.

332
00:23:05,620 --> 00:23:08,530
Su Ah, is Grandma doing well?

333
00:23:09,090 --> 00:23:10,730
And Great-Grandma and Grandma Ri Ja?

334
00:23:10,890 --> 00:23:11,900
Yes.

335
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:16,200
But Mom, you know what?
Uncle Dae Chi...

336
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:18,400
Uncle Dae Chi?

337
00:23:19,100 --> 00:23:20,400
What about Uncle Dae Chi?

338
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:23,510
He said there was another uncle
picking fights with him.

339
00:23:24,840 --> 00:23:25,840
Picking fights?

340
00:23:26,510 --> 00:23:27,510
Yes.

341
00:23:27,880 --> 00:23:29,910
He must be
a really scary uncle, Mom.

342
00:23:30,250 --> 00:23:32,450
The whole family was so shocked.

343
00:23:32,980 --> 00:23:35,750
Because of that uncle
picking fights,

344
00:23:35,950 --> 00:23:37,790
Grandma drank a lot of makgeolli.

345
00:23:38,790 --> 00:23:41,390
Dae Chi isn't the type
to get into fights with anyone.

346
00:23:42,330 --> 00:23:44,230
Did he get into a parking dispute
or something?

347
00:23:48,430 --> 00:23:49,670
You startled me.

348
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:51,300
What are you doing here?

349
00:23:54,600 --> 00:23:55,710
I'm sorry, Su Ah.

350
00:23:56,210 --> 00:23:57,840
Dad accidentally fell asleep.

351
00:23:58,240 --> 00:24:00,980
I meant to get up right away
to go pick you up.

352
00:24:08,250 --> 00:24:09,250
Su Ah,

353
00:24:09,350 --> 00:24:11,820
Dad has something
to talk about with Mom,

354
00:24:12,020 --> 00:24:13,490
so could you go inside first?

355
00:24:13,820 --> 00:24:16,890
Okay, I like it
when you two talk to each other.

356
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:18,260
I really like it.

357
00:24:29,970 --> 00:24:31,310
Unbelievable.

358
00:24:32,010 --> 00:24:33,440
When are you going
to get your act together?

359
00:24:33,610 --> 00:24:36,150
I'm trying to get it together
starting right now, okay?

360
00:24:37,480 --> 00:24:39,950
Someone has to believe you, right?

361
00:24:40,850 --> 00:24:43,690
Don't worry,
our daughter Su Ah believes me.

362
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:48,560
Do you have any idea
what I'm thinking of doing?

363
00:24:49,990 --> 00:24:51,830
After hearing what you said
in front of the kindergarten,

364
00:24:52,300 --> 00:24:53,360
I'm actually...

365
00:24:54,100 --> 00:24:58,500
thinking about making
a pretty big decision right now.

366
00:25:01,810 --> 00:25:02,840
Why?

367
00:25:03,940 --> 00:25:05,640
- What?
- By the way,

368
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:08,040
did Dae Chi get into
a parking dispute or something?

369
00:25:08,510 --> 00:25:09,580
A parking dispute?

370
00:25:09,950 --> 00:25:11,350
What are you talking about
all of a sudden?

371
00:25:11,650 --> 00:25:12,920
Su Ah said she heard about it.

372
00:25:13,280 --> 00:25:14,720
She told me when we got back
just now.

373
00:25:15,150 --> 00:25:16,150
Su Ah did?

374
00:25:17,350 --> 00:25:19,690
No, nothing like that happened.

375
00:25:20,460 --> 00:25:21,960
If it's not a parking dispute,

376
00:25:22,490 --> 00:25:25,360
is there someone at work
who's bothering your brother?

377
00:25:25,860 --> 00:25:27,430
She said there was an uncle
picking fights with him.

378
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:29,230
What are you talking about?

379
00:25:29,630 --> 00:25:31,500
Who would be foolish enough
to pick a fight with him?

380
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:34,870
So you're saying
nothing is wrong with your brother?

381
00:25:35,310 --> 00:25:37,640
Hey, as for something
being wrong with him...

382
00:25:39,940 --> 00:25:40,980
There actually...

383
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:42,880
is something.

384
00:25:43,580 --> 00:25:46,050
Something incredibly huge.

385
00:25:47,280 --> 00:25:48,290
Why?

386
00:25:48,920 --> 00:25:50,020
Do you want to know?

387
00:25:52,860 --> 00:25:54,720
No, why would I?

388
00:25:55,230 --> 00:25:56,730
I'm not a part
of this family anymore.

389
00:25:56,830 --> 00:25:58,330
That's what I'm saying.

390
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:01,500
I have the evening shift today,
so I'm leaving.

391
00:26:02,370 --> 00:26:05,570
- Yes, I'm not stopping you.
- Make sure Su Ah eats well.

392
00:26:05,840 --> 00:26:07,100
And make sure she brushes her teeth.

393
00:26:08,040 --> 00:26:09,740
Who do you think you are?

394
00:26:10,610 --> 00:26:12,410
You're not getting
any sleep tonight.

395
00:26:12,640 --> 00:26:13,640
Please.

396
00:26:15,150 --> 00:26:16,480
When did you get so soft?

397
00:26:36,930 --> 00:26:37,930
Right.

398
00:26:38,770 --> 00:26:40,300
I'll do my part,

399
00:26:41,370 --> 00:26:43,370
so make sure you do your part
someday too.

400
00:26:52,020 --> 00:26:53,450
I'm not giving up on this.

401
00:26:54,620 --> 00:26:57,490
Whether it's Paris or New York,
design school is...

402
00:26:58,490 --> 00:27:00,020
definitely not something
I'm giving up on.

403
00:27:00,960 --> 00:27:02,190
I'm just postponing it
for a while...

404
00:27:03,830 --> 00:27:05,400
(Haedeul Bank)

405
00:27:05,460 --> 00:27:07,060
to protect my family.

406
00:27:17,440 --> 00:27:19,340
(Sibling 2)

407
00:27:24,810 --> 00:27:26,520
- Come out.
- What?

408
00:27:27,280 --> 00:27:29,090
What do you mean, come out?
Where are you?

409
00:27:29,950 --> 00:27:32,060
I'm in front of your office,
so come out right now.

410
00:27:34,420 --> 00:27:35,430
My office?

411
00:27:35,660 --> 00:27:37,360
Are you really in front
of my office? Really?

412
00:27:38,330 --> 00:27:39,500
I told you I am.

413
00:27:39,900 --> 00:27:41,330
Come out
while I'm still feeling generous.

414
00:27:41,870 --> 00:27:44,070
Really? Kkangda, are you serious?

415
00:27:44,600 --> 00:27:45,640
You're not lying, right?

416
00:27:47,640 --> 00:27:49,810
Come out if you want to get
your money, you fool.

417
00:27:58,720 --> 00:28:00,850
(Haedeul Bank)

418
00:28:12,960 --> 00:28:14,930
(Mission: Mompossible)

419
00:28:15,070 --> 00:28:17,930
They should have
rice and kimchi, right?

420
00:28:18,300 --> 00:28:20,800
Who cares?

421
00:28:22,210 --> 00:28:24,670
- Dad, what's that?
- This is Kkangda's, isn't it?

422
00:28:24,740 --> 00:28:26,580
Are you out of your mind?
Don't you want the money?

423
00:28:27,180 --> 00:28:28,810
Isn't this
Manager Kang Da Mi's phone?

424
00:28:28,880 --> 00:28:29,880
Who did you say you were?

425
00:28:30,810 --> 00:28:32,780
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
